What the project is
A full-stack web application that automatically analyzes drone flight logs and generates professional PDF crash/health reports. A user uploads a raw flight log from the browser; the backend detects the log format, parses the binary/text data, runs ~50+ diagnostic checks across flight phases, and returns a downloadable PDF with charts, a flight-path map, and pass/warn/fail findings — including the probable cause of a crash.

It supports two drone ecosystems: ArduPilot (.bin) and JIYI K++ agricultural drones (binary + text logs), with automatic format detection by reading file magic-byte headers.

Architecture (what you actually built)
Frontend — App.tsx

React 19 + TypeScript + Vite, styled with Tailwind CSS
File upload UI, calls the backend, parses the Content-Disposition header to name the PDF, and gives view/download options
Backend — main.py

FastAPI service with a /analyze endpoint and a /health check
CORS middleware, file-size limits (500 MB), extension allow-listing, async upload handling
Format auto-detection via binary magic bytes (0xA3 0x95 for ArduPilot, 0x00 0xFF / 0x37 0xC8 for JIYI), plus a printable-ASCII heuristic to tell text logs from binary
XOR decryption of encrypted JIYI logs
Calls a Windows .NET converter (binToLog.exe) under Mono + Xvfb (headless virtual display) inside Linux to convert proprietary JIYI binaries
An asyncio.Lock to serialize the converter, per-job temp directories, UUID job IDs, and background cleanup tasks
Analysis engines — ardupilot_report.py (~3,600 lines) + jiyi_report.py (~3,100 lines)

Custom binary log parser written from scratch — reads the ArduPilot/DataFlash self-describing format (FMT messages), unpacks each message type with Python struct, applies field scaling, decodes strings
GPS-week → IST real-time clock reconstruction so report timestamps show actual wall-clock time
A FlightAnalysis engine running phased diagnostic checks: clean boot, power stability, battery voltage (cell-count aware), IMU detection/health/vibration/clipping, compass field & interference, GPS fix/satellites/HDOP, EKF readiness/variance/lane-switch/yaw, RC signal loss, arming & safety-bypass checks, failsafes, hardware-spike detection, and more
PDF report generation with ReportLab + Matplotlib charts (flight path, altitude, voltage, vibration, attitude) and color-coded PASS/WARN/FAIL tables
Heavy defensive data-cleaning of corrupt sensor records (timestamp sanity caps, physical-range filtering)
